WEBVTT

00:05.720 --> 00:09.370
Sunraku-san... still hasn't returned.

00:16.340 --> 00:20.540
Which means... he's still fighting.

00:22.690 --> 00:24.240
Sunraku-san!

01:59.100 --> 02:03.980
I guess we'll need more than stat 
boosts to make a breakthrough here.

02:04.470 --> 02:07.230
Its armor seems thickest around the waist.

02:07.710 --> 02:10.490
That's probably where all the 
important bits are stored...

02:10.930 --> 02:15.740
But how the heck do we 
go about prying it open?

02:16.210 --> 02:21.750
<b>Putting Feelings Into a Moment, Part 4</b>

02:17.220 --> 02:19.810
I've got an idea.

02:19.810 --> 02:20.860
Are you in?

02:20.860 --> 02:21.750
An idea?

02:22.430 --> 02:25.170
A sure-fire plan to break through 
Kirin Armor's outer shell.

02:25.920 --> 02:26.880
I call it...

02:27.370 --> 02:30.120
Clear Sky Conquest.

02:30.740 --> 02:33.670
That which can cleave even dragons...

02:36.720 --> 02:38.680
Sky Clear!

02:36.840 --> 02:38.670
<b>Sky Clear</b>

02:49.430 --> 02:51.210
<i>What the heck was that?</i>

02:51.960 --> 02:54.240
<i>"Sky Clear," he called it, I guess...</i>

02:55.220 --> 02:56.830
<i>But this move is...</i>

02:58.740 --> 03:00.530
<i>way too nasty.</i>

03:05.950 --> 03:07.110
Will it reach?!

03:07.110 --> 03:07.880
Wait!

03:16.560 --> 03:18.890
<i>But it's like I told you...</i>

03:20.780 --> 03:24.180
<i>It's gonna take more than that to beat me!</i>

03:22.300 --> 03:25.600
<b>Rebirth Tearjewel</b>

03:31.940 --> 03:35.150
My ultimate technique, the self-revive!

03:35.150 --> 03:38.580
<i>It was a huge gamble, but I managed to 
time it just right to revive myself!</i>

03:39.080 --> 03:40.830
<i>Still, my equipment's not so lucky...</i>

03:41.180 --> 03:43.120
<i>My Spiked Battlehelm is half trashed.</i>

03:43.120 --> 03:46.120
<i>My Lifestide Sash is totally kaput.</i>

03:46.950 --> 03:49.210
<i>That "Clear Sky" move</i>

03:49.680 --> 03:50.630
<i>is nasty.</i>

03:55.240 --> 03:58.140
<i>So it's got equipment-destroying 
and armor-piercing effects...</i>

03:58.970 --> 04:00.970
<i>Maybe the Insta-Death effect, too?</i>

04:02.040 --> 04:03.340
But...

04:05.030 --> 04:07.450
Until you surpass my ultimate,

04:07.450 --> 04:10.230
I shall not fall.

04:11.410 --> 04:13.020
<i>That stance again!</i>

04:13.560 --> 04:15.330
Clear Sky Conquest...

04:15.940 --> 04:17.040
Thunderclap!

04:18.770 --> 04:20.020
<i>Hang on a damn minute!</i>

04:20.020 --> 04:22.320
<i>We're back to the attack spam?!</i>

04:25.700 --> 04:26.700
Wind Slash.

04:27.970 --> 04:29.130
Wind Slash.

04:29.970 --> 04:31.040
Wind Slash.

04:31.560 --> 04:32.710
<i>Too damn close!</i>

04:34.070 --> 04:35.300
I get it.

04:35.300 --> 04:38.010
<i>That chain of attacks and 
the final Sky Clear move...</i>

04:38.720 --> 04:41.590
<i>All of it together makes 
up "Clear Sky Conquest."</i>

04:42.030 --> 04:45.310
<i>So... how do I solve it?</i>

04:44.090 --> 04:45.300
<b>Sky Clear</b>

04:45.720 --> 04:50.470
<i>Last time, it took about thirty 
seconds before the Sky Clear hit me.</i>

04:50.470 --> 04:51.310
Pyroclastic Wyrm.

04:53.460 --> 04:55.730
<i>There's lag time before 
Pyroclastic Wyrm activates.</i>

04:55.960 --> 04:57.810
<i>That one's not a huge threat.</i>

04:58.770 --> 05:00.420
Ash Blizzard.

05:02.840 --> 05:04.580
<i>Same with Ash Blizzard.</i>

05:04.580 --> 05:07.010
<i>It's easy to dodge when I know it's coming!</i>

05:08.290 --> 05:09.510
Tidal Rush.

05:10.390 --> 05:13.790
<i>The moves he uses in Clear Sky 
Conquest might be chosen at random,</i>

05:14.410 --> 05:16.550
<i>but the actual dodging 
is a memorization game!</i>

05:16.860 --> 05:17.960
Wind Slash.

05:18.880 --> 05:21.090
<i>Given all the moves in his arsenal,</i>

05:21.090 --> 05:22.480
<i>the go-to strategy is to</i>

05:22.480 --> 05:25.930
<i>preserve stamina and keep about 
three meters from him at all times.</i>

05:26.220 --> 05:27.640
Thunderclap.

05:28.640 --> 05:30.640
<i>Keep your movements to the bare minimum.</i>

05:31.240 --> 05:33.560
<i>This isn't so scary once you get used to it.</i>

05:35.680 --> 05:36.570
<i>He got my leg again!</i>

05:37.660 --> 05:38.350
<u>Use Items</u>
Rebirth Tearjewel
 Divine Lifesalve
Potion
 High Potion

05:38.870 --> 05:40.170
<i>It's thirty seconds, for sure.</i>

05:42.150 --> 05:43.660
<i>Now, here's the real challenge...</i>

05:43.650 --> 05:45.070
<b>Sky                                                                 Clear</b>

05:43.990 --> 05:45.070
Sky Clear!

05:46.340 --> 05:49.500
<i>He's killed me plenty of times before, 
but this one feels different.</i>

05:49.840 --> 05:51.250
<i>It's more fundamentally...</i>

05:51.990 --> 05:56.720
<i>an insta-kill attack, meant to slaughter 
the player without you getting a say.</i>

06:04.850 --> 06:05.640
<i>I'll bet...</i>

06:06.580 --> 06:10.120
<i>Even if a level 99 player buffed 
their defenses with full armor</i>

06:10.120 --> 06:11.640
<i>and a shield at the ready,</i>

06:12.230 --> 06:15.900
<i>he'd still split them in 
half like a block of tofu.</i>

06:16.170 --> 06:18.800
Until you surpass my ultimate,

06:19.610 --> 06:22.280
I shall not fall.

06:22.870 --> 06:24.910
Clear Sky Conquest!

06:31.200 --> 06:34.750
<i>And the worst part of all is 
that he keeps you from dodging!</i>

06:35.420 --> 06:38.060
<i>Once you're rooted to the spot like that,</i>

06:38.060 --> 06:40.550
<i>you don't have a choice but 
to soak his Sky Clear attack.</i>

06:42.550 --> 06:43.840
Sky Clear!

06:44.990 --> 06:46.720
<i>Destroy his sword?</i>

06:46.720 --> 06:51.650
<i>No, that's not a realistic option when 
you're dodging the attack spam...</i>

06:51.650 --> 06:53.430
<i>Same with taking down the guy himself.</i>

06:58.390 --> 07:00.980
<u>Use Items</u>
Divine Lifesalve
Potion
 High Potion

06:58.400 --> 07:00.980
<i>That was my last Rebirth Tearjewel.</i>

07:01.240 --> 07:03.740
<i>All I've got left are five Divine Lifesalves.</i>

07:04.130 --> 07:06.440
<i>If the Sky Clear comes every thirty seconds,</i>

07:06.850 --> 07:09.400
<i>that means I've got three 
minutes left to live.</i>

07:09.840 --> 07:12.760
<i>It's been less than five 
minutes since Phase 3 started.</i>

07:12.760 --> 07:14.000
<i>I won't make it to ten.</i>

07:14.340 --> 07:17.060
Until you surpass my ultimate,

07:17.060 --> 07:19.500
I shall not fall.

07:20.480 --> 07:23.770
<i>Until I "surpass" it... he won't fall?</i>

07:25.780 --> 07:27.600
Clear Sky Conquest.

07:27.600 --> 07:28.510
Wind Slash!

07:32.290 --> 07:33.270
Thunderclap!

07:35.170 --> 07:39.280
<i>But then, the "survive ten minutes" 
thing was just a theory from the start.</i>

07:39.630 --> 07:45.110
<i>Right now, I'm thinking "survive the Clear 
Sky Conquest" is a more likely scenario.</i>

07:49.470 --> 07:50.240
Sky Clear!

07:52.580 --> 07:57.560
<i>Solving the Sky Clear must be the 
victory condition against Wethermon!</i>

07:58.530 --> 08:02.290
<i>And the key to doing that 
has gotta be to parry.</i>

08:03.020 --> 08:05.100
<i>Against an opponent of Wethermon's caliber,</i>

08:05.100 --> 08:08.050
<i>you'd need to deflect with 
the timing of a critical...</i>

08:08.050 --> 08:10.270
<i>You've gotta do it while rooted to one spot,</i>

08:10.270 --> 08:14.060
<i>in a state where you can't 
make any stance adjustments.</i>

08:14.490 --> 08:18.300
<i>If you get the timing off by a millisecond, 
he'll shatter your weapon.</i>

08:18.300 --> 08:22.060
<i>Still, it's the only way to win.</i>

08:22.060 --> 08:29.070
Climax Boost

08:22.060 --> 08:29.070
Hunger Wolf

08:22.060 --> 08:29.070
Vorpal Blade Tech
[Moon's Reflection]

08:22.480 --> 08:25.860
<i>My job right now is to work out 
what I need in that final moment,</i>

08:25.860 --> 08:29.070
<i>and make sure I have it at my disposal.</i>

08:31.940 --> 08:33.700
<i>Sunraku</i>

08:32.390 --> 08:33.700
<i>Soon.</i>

08:33.910 --> 08:35.580
<i>Soon, I'll have everything I need...</i>

08:36.020 --> 08:38.080
<i>Wait just a little while longer...</i>

08:38.680 --> 08:39.870
<i>Wethermon.</i>

08:40.330 --> 08:43.210
Until you surpass my ultimate,

08:43.210 --> 08:45.790
I shall not fall.

08:58.390 --> 09:01.230
Let Sunraku-kun handle all that.

09:01.230 --> 09:05.690
Yeah, we've got our own job to focus on.

09:05.690 --> 09:11.360
Now, as far as your sure-fire way 
to take down Kirin Armor goes...

09:11.600 --> 09:15.120
It's not gonna be easy to 
get him where we need him.

09:15.120 --> 09:16.620
Can't do it, hmm?

09:16.620 --> 09:18.080
Oh, please.

09:18.080 --> 09:20.620
Don't go underestimating a fighting game pro.

09:20.830 --> 09:22.020
In that case...

09:22.620 --> 09:23.920
Get on that.

09:24.020 --> 09:24.630
<i>Pencilgon</i>

09:27.920 --> 09:30.130
Wh-Why'd you just kill yourself?!

09:45.310 --> 09:47.360
That took forever!

09:47.360 --> 09:48.670
What's wrong with you?

09:48.670 --> 09:51.040
H-Hey, that's my line!

09:51.040 --> 09:54.990
A spear-wielder can't 
fight with just one hand.

09:54.990 --> 09:57.130
But resurrection sets me back to normal.

09:57.130 --> 09:59.330
At least warn me first!

09:59.690 --> 10:02.830
Now, let's start again fresh!

10:03.630 --> 10:05.750
<i>First, gotta find its weak spot...</i>

10:08.340 --> 10:11.000
<i>The backbone linking the 
top and bottom portions!</i>

10:11.000 --> 10:13.220
<i>It feels just like the other parts!</i>

10:13.630 --> 10:15.570
Hey, hey! I'm right over here!

10:17.150 --> 10:19.890
Not as easy to shake off this time, am I?

10:20.150 --> 10:22.600
I've drugged myself into a major buff stack,

10:22.960 --> 10:25.230
<i>and</i> I'm using two whips!

10:28.170 --> 10:31.860
The second you lift up 
the leg, the body falls!

10:32.430 --> 10:35.410
Katzo-kun, well done!

10:35.410 --> 10:38.060
If you wanna be a fighting 
game pro in the VR game age,

10:38.060 --> 10:44.920
you'd better know how the human body 
moves under any set of circumstances!

10:44.920 --> 10:46.570
This thing isn't really human!

10:46.570 --> 10:49.880
It's humanoid! Basically the same thing!

10:51.380 --> 10:54.170
Okay, and that's when...

10:57.090 --> 10:58.860
I add more whips!

10:58.860 --> 11:02.770
I've got you wrapped up 
in every whip I've got!

11:03.850 --> 11:05.800
<i>I suppose that's the end of this weapon.</i>

11:03.850 --> 11:06.190
<b>Twisted Steel Spear
 Category: Spear
 Durability:
 Attribute: Corrode</b>

11:03.850 --> 11:06.190
<b>Breakage Warning
 Weapon change recommended</b>

11:06.190 --> 11:12.070
<i>Adding armor-piercing buffs to your weapons 
wears down their durability very quickly.</i>

11:12.670 --> 11:17.840
<i>I've hit its back, arms, and legs multiple 
times over the course of the fight,</i>

11:17.840 --> 11:20.280
<i>but it's just as tough all over.</i>

11:20.700 --> 11:25.220
<i>Still... there's one place where the 
armor is tougher than the others.</i>

11:25.750 --> 11:28.710
<i>That waist of yours is just too suspicious!</i>

11:28.950 --> 11:30.710
Katzo-kun! Move it forward!

11:30.940 --> 11:32.220
Got it!

11:33.490 --> 11:35.220
I won't be able to hold it for long!

11:35.220 --> 11:36.470
Okay!

11:36.970 --> 11:40.220
It's time to spill your guts, giant!

11:41.150 --> 11:42.990
Spear of Sunlight!

11:41.970 --> 11:43.970
Spear of Sunlight

11:41.970 --> 11:43.970
Spear of Sunlight

11:45.230 --> 11:46.310
<b>Weapon Durability Depleted
 Breakage Warning
 Weapon change recommended</b>

11:46.580 --> 11:48.560
Come on, you can hang in 
there a little longer!

11:48.820 --> 11:51.700
My buffs are about to run out, y'know!

11:58.200 --> 11:59.450
I got it off!

11:59.450 --> 12:02.120
Great! Then, let's finish the job!

12:08.870 --> 12:10.470
It shredded all my whips!

12:19.300 --> 12:21.990
The hell is this? A berserker mode?!

12:21.990 --> 12:25.500
Looks like breaking the 
waist armor set it off!

12:25.500 --> 12:27.230
What's the plan? Fall back for a bit?

12:27.230 --> 12:29.730
No, we press the attack.

12:29.730 --> 12:31.380
If we just let it rampage,

12:31.380 --> 12:36.230
one of those indiscriminate beams 
or missiles might hit Sunraku-kun.

12:36.800 --> 12:40.180
I think you can imagine 
what that would lead to.

12:41.050 --> 12:43.060
Huh? What was that?

12:43.060 --> 12:45.550
While I was going toe-to-toe 
with a unique monster,

12:45.550 --> 12:49.920
<i>someone</i> couldn't even handle 
distracting his pet horse?!

12:49.920 --> 12:53.130
I'd sure love to hear <i>all</i> about that!

12:55.660 --> 12:58.920
We'll be in for six months of <i>that</i>.

12:58.920 --> 13:01.160
No doubt. I'd do the same thing.

13:01.160 --> 13:02.370
Yeah, so would I.

13:03.060 --> 13:04.060
Okay!

13:04.060 --> 13:07.770
In that case, we've done all our prep...

13:07.970 --> 13:10.410
So let's seal the deal 
on your sure-fire plan!

13:10.410 --> 13:11.770
You said it.

13:11.770 --> 13:14.720
Time for Giant Killing!

13:23.890 --> 13:26.540
<i>I only have two spears left.</i>

13:26.540 --> 13:29.250
Boy, what a waste.

13:29.250 --> 13:32.400
Do you know how much it 
costs to make one of these?

13:32.400 --> 13:35.100
Now's not the time to get stingy!

13:36.290 --> 13:39.050
Must be nice to just use your fists...

13:40.730 --> 13:41.550
Okay...

13:43.380 --> 13:45.050
Thou art that which binds.

13:45.490 --> 13:47.310
I am that which holds fast.

13:47.560 --> 13:49.060
<i>I merge with all of creation.</i>

13:49.620 --> 13:52.220
<i>I find the incompatible darkness...</i>

13:52.940 --> 13:54.060
<i>and strike!</i>

14:01.840 --> 14:03.740
Shadow Wedge!

14:08.200 --> 14:09.590
Shadow Wedge...

14:10.510 --> 14:12.790
It's a spell that lets you 
seal a target in place

14:12.790 --> 14:16.260
by stabbing your weapon into its shadow.

14:17.210 --> 14:20.290
It lasts until the weapon breaks.

14:21.140 --> 14:24.550
Given Kirin's size, that'll probably 
be about five seconds from now.

14:25.350 --> 14:27.100
We only get one chance at this!

14:27.430 --> 14:30.290
Let's go... my last spear!

14:31.410 --> 14:35.060
Giant Killing Skewer!

14:35.060 --> 14:37.060
Giant Killing Skewer

14:35.060 --> 14:38.060
Giant Killing Skewer

14:38.580 --> 14:41.300
Perfect for a mammoth like 
this, don't you think?!

14:41.880 --> 14:43.550
It's time, Katzo-kun!

14:43.550 --> 14:45.910
Okay! Hold it tight!

14:49.030 --> 14:50.040
Pencilgon!

14:51.020 --> 14:51.790
<i>Drat.</i>

14:52.210 --> 14:54.790
<i>It fired a missile before I locked it down?</i>

14:59.460 --> 15:01.290
Damn it...

15:00.040 --> 15:02.350
That's no problem!

15:07.230 --> 15:11.780
I said that a spear-wielder 
can't fight with only one arm...

15:12.210 --> 15:14.180
but I take that back.

15:15.410 --> 15:17.430
Kirin Armor...

15:17.950 --> 15:20.690
I only need one arm for you!

15:21.480 --> 15:25.490
Go! Giant Killing!

15:27.820 --> 15:31.070
All or Nothing

15:27.820 --> 15:31.070
All or Nothing

15:28.900 --> 15:31.080
All or Nothing!

15:34.800 --> 15:37.250
It's all yours, Katzo-kun.

15:40.730 --> 15:43.090
Red, Blue, Yellow.

15:43.090 --> 15:44.870
Three colors merge.

15:45.730 --> 15:48.470
Spirit Fist: Dark Overstrike!

15:49.390 --> 15:53.280
Just go down already, you empty shell!

15:53.850 --> 15:58.600
Human Pile Bunker!

16:03.240 --> 16:04.030
Katzo-kun!

16:25.730 --> 16:27.010
I'm 'kay.

16:40.040 --> 16:44.500
Boy, I'm tired!

16:44.500 --> 16:46.780
We were so screwed if 
that hadn't clinched it!

16:48.380 --> 16:51.520
I'm so drained from Dark Overstrike 
that I can't move a muscle.

16:51.520 --> 16:53.170
You're out of stamina.

16:53.170 --> 16:54.780
Rest for a while and you'll—

16:55.790 --> 16:56.910
How's Sunraku-kun?!

17:07.420 --> 17:10.350
That was my last resurrection item.

17:10.740 --> 17:13.040
I made it in time, Wethermon.

17:13.040 --> 17:14.680
I've got everything I need now.

17:14.990 --> 17:16.460
Hungry Wolf.

17:17.460 --> 17:19.060
Climax Boost.

17:20.100 --> 17:22.560
Their recast time is over.

17:22.560 --> 17:26.440
<b>Moonblade
Combination Possible</b>

17:23.630 --> 17:26.440
And my Moonblades' fusion gauge is filled up.

17:28.850 --> 17:31.030
Clear Sky Conquest!

17:32.560 --> 17:34.450
In thirty seconds

17:32.950 --> 17:34.450
<b>Head Equipment Changed</b>

17:33.420 --> 17:34.450
<b>Staring Bird Mask</b>

17:34.730 --> 17:36.980
you'll dish out your last Sky Clear.

17:37.440 --> 17:39.080
Wethermon the Tombguard...

17:39.690 --> 17:41.830
I'm gonna solve your ultimate strike

17:41.830 --> 17:45.840
and bring on the finale!

17:42.830 --> 17:45.830
<b>Moonblade
Combination Possible</b>

17:47.460 --> 17:48.470
Wind Slash!

17:52.440 --> 17:53.510
Tidal Rush!

17:55.560 --> 17:56.640
Nimbus Fist!

18:03.270 --> 18:04.900
<i>I'm using my recast time</i>

18:05.530 --> 18:08.650
<i>to identify exactly how long his 
Clear Sky Conquest has been going.</i>

18:06.890 --> 18:08.270
Climax Boost

18:06.890 --> 18:08.270
Hunger Wolf

18:06.890 --> 18:08.650
Vorpal Blade Tech
[Moon's Reflection]

18:08.650 --> 18:10.410
Vorpal Blade Tech
[Moon's Reflection]

18:09.070 --> 18:10.820
<i>The Sky Clear is coming in two seconds.</i>

18:11.400 --> 18:13.170
It'll be your last Sky Clear...

18:13.170 --> 18:14.570
Bring it on, Wethermon!

18:14.970 --> 18:17.860
<i>The key to beating it is the Moonblade...</i>

18:23.050 --> 18:24.650
Twin Moon!

18:25.350 --> 18:32.130
<b>Moonblade 
Twin Moon</b>

18:25.570 --> 18:28.000
<i>The fusion of the blades 
"Waxing" and "Waning."</i>

18:28.400 --> 18:29.910
<i>It comes with a special effect:</i>

18:29.910 --> 18:34.400
<i>the lower your stats are, 
relative to your enemy's,</i>

18:34.400 --> 18:37.800
<i>the greater the power and 
likelihood of your criticals.</i>

18:38.200 --> 18:40.890
<i>It's the best weapon possible 
for these circumstances.</i>

18:41.530 --> 18:44.150
<i>It raises the likelihood 
that my parry will work!</i>

18:44.520 --> 18:45.190
<i>And...</i>

18:45.600 --> 18:49.030
<i>With the stacked effects of 
Climax Boost and Hunger Wolf,</i>

18:49.030 --> 18:50.860
<i>I'll raise my action speed!</i>

18:51.310 --> 18:54.450
<i>With all this, I can block 
his Sky Clear for sure!</i>

18:56.110 --> 18:58.450
<b>Climax Boost</b>

18:56.110 --> 18:58.450
<b>Cannot Activate</b>

18:57.620 --> 18:58.990
I can't activate it?

18:58.990 --> 19:00.750
<i>Sunraku</i>

19:01.110 --> 19:05.250
<i>I've got a skill I can only activate 
when my HP fall below one-third—</i>

19:06.040 --> 19:08.260
<i>I screwed up!</i>

19:08.260 --> 19:11.750
<i>How'd I manage to blow my prep like this?!</i>

19:12.000 --> 19:12.990
<i>I'm doomed!</i>

19:12.990 --> 19:14.990
<i>I've soaked that attack 
enough times to know...</i>

19:14.990 --> 19:18.120
<i>Hunger Wolf alone won't let 
me match the attack speed!</i>

19:18.120 --> 19:20.010
<i>Think, man! There's gotta be a way!</i>

19:20.010 --> 19:22.130
<i>Sunraku, think!</i>

19:22.130 --> 19:24.120
<i>Think up a way!</i>

19:24.120 --> 19:24.770
Sky—

19:38.160 --> 19:41.910
<i>You guys are all so obsessed 
with that Setsuna lady...</i>

19:45.080 --> 19:48.180
<i>Today's major update changed 
the activation conditions</i>

19:48.180 --> 19:50.390
<i>for the luck-based "Endure" status...</i>

19:51.040 --> 19:53.360
<i>If your luck stat is over fifty,</i>

19:53.360 --> 19:58.100
<i>and your HP reaches zero due to 
self-inflicted or recoil damage,</i>

19:56.630 --> 19:59.260
<b>Endure</b>

19:58.100 --> 20:02.420
<i>Just once, you can hang 
in there with a single HP!</i>

20:03.130 --> 20:04.680
<i>Sunraku</i>

20:04.860 --> 20:05.430
<b>Hunger Wolf
</b>STR, AGI, and VIT increase
in proportion to hunger and low HP,
but reduces Stamina, DEX, and TEC in exchange.

20:05.570 --> 20:06.140
<b>Climax Boost
</b>All stats increase in proportion
to level deficiency against enemy.

20:09.940 --> 20:13.810
Clear Sky Conquest is a chain of 
actions that concludes with Sky Clear.

20:14.310 --> 20:19.530
In other words, until you release your 
Sky Clear, you'll never give up...

20:20.970 --> 20:23.210
Either on the Clear Sky Conquest action

20:23.210 --> 20:25.790
or your oath to guard that 
grave forever and ever!

20:26.800 --> 20:30.330
On behalf of Vash, I'm putting you down!

20:30.590 --> 20:31.830
Sky Clear!

20:32.590 --> 20:35.010
Crescent Vorpal!

20:37.840 --> 20:40.340
Crescent Vorpal

20:37.840 --> 20:40.340
Crescent Vorpal

20:37.860 --> 20:40.340
<b>Sky Clear</b>

20:43.630 --> 20:45.350
Go to sleep already...

20:45.670 --> 20:48.590
Wethermon the Tombguard!

20:56.310 --> 20:58.430
You were really strong...

20:58.430 --> 21:01.910
But I've seen enough of your 
attacks for a lifetime...

21:03.710 --> 21:06.340
And your blade won't reach me ever again.

21:09.650 --> 21:13.420
The ultimate strike has been solved.

21:22.680 --> 21:23.930
Brilliant.

21:26.800 --> 21:30.940
You have broken through my ultimate strike.

21:33.270 --> 21:38.190
As "Clear Sky" transformed into 
my ultimate, "Sky Clear"...

21:40.170 --> 21:43.920
So, again, do the words transform... 
to describe your talent.

21:56.640 --> 21:58.530
"It is as clear as a cloudless sky."

23:41.890 --> 23:49.150
<b>SLF Mini</b>

23:42.670 --> 23:45.680
<i>SLF</i> Theater!

23:45.680 --> 23:49.150
<i><b>The Saiga Family Valentine</b></i>

23:46.480 --> 23:47.910
Mini!

23:49.150 --> 25:22.250
<i><b>SLF Theater</b></i>

23:50.020 --> 23:52.550
First, I got some chocolate bars.

23:52.900 --> 23:55.520
Then I chopped it up.

23:55.960 --> 23:59.040
Then I melted it with a water bath.

23:59.400 --> 24:01.220
That all went as planned.

24:01.220 --> 24:04.340
But what shape should I make them?

24:04.650 --> 24:08.550
Valentine's Day chocolate for Hizutome-kun...

24:08.990 --> 24:12.440
A-Am I really ready to give him hearts?

24:12.440 --> 24:15.180
Well... maybe I should use that shape, then?

24:17.970 --> 24:22.620
But just giving him his own head 
would be annoying to him...

24:22.620 --> 24:28.170
And giving him half-naked chocolate 
might be a little embarrassing...

24:28.720 --> 24:29.590
In that case...

24:31.110 --> 24:34.280
Oh, Hizutome-kun would eat me?!

24:34.280 --> 24:36.930
It's definitely way too soon for that!

24:36.930 --> 24:39.870
No, no! Don't nibble me there!

24:39.870 --> 24:41.910
Y-You're going to start there?

24:41.910 --> 24:44.500
You're filling your mouth? That loudly?!

24:44.500 --> 24:46.630
We're both underage!

24:47.170 --> 24:49.210
No, it's no good.

24:49.210 --> 24:51.500
I'll need to use a different shape.

24:51.500 --> 24:54.330
It's too much for me, emotionally.

24:54.330 --> 24:55.600
I-In that case...

24:56.640 --> 24:58.160
I'll make it my sister!

24:58.600 --> 25:00.170
But why?!

25:00.170 --> 25:04.110
I've got myself so confused!

25:04.960 --> 25:06.630
In that case...

25:10.870 --> 25:16.870
I melted it in the water bath, 
then reshaped it back into chocolate bars!

25:17.790 --> 25:22.250
<b>Even though it was tastier than store-bought, the fact
that it looked exactly like store-bought made it creepier. 
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hBy Mana Iwamaki</b>
